  "$comment_later": "buildings, stations, characters and pals are appended by their phases; the schema test only validates sections that exist and are non-empty.",
  "$comment_buildings": "Composites/props are baked to world size in the pipeline, so scale here is a retune knob that defaults to 1. `houses.variants[0]` (house_a) is always the player's own home, the one house with an interior and a working door; every other ring slot cycles through `village.variants`, whole prebuilt Quaternius buildings with no door (docs/decisions/D62). Dressing is placed verbatim in village-local metres; collider 0 means walk-through. Stones stretch the shipped menhir props: scaleXZ/scaleY are [min,max] ranges the seeded rng picks inside, so girth stays near the primitive silhouette the 1.1 collider was tuned for.",
  "buildings": {
    "$comment_houses_door": "Per-variant doorway anchor in the house's own local frame (front is -z, same convention Hall.ts uses). x/z/width/height are metres, measured from the wall-doorway-square aperture baked into each composite by scripts/asset-jobs.mjs (the kit's 0.4x0.75-tile hole, scaled by the house's baked-in composite scale) and z is the front wall's plane. yaw is the leaf's closed-facing rotation added on top of the house's own yaw, 0 for a leaf that swings out of a wall running along local x.",
    "houses": {
      "variants": [
        {
          "url": "models/buildings/house_a.glb",
          "scale": 1.0,
